 ### Touch controls (Android)
 
-On a phone or tablet an on-screen overlay appears in the margins beside the game picture: a black C64-style joystick bottom-left (eight directions), and two red buttons bottom-right, **FIRE** (the # fire key) and **SPACE** (next weapon), so moving and attacking work with two thumbs. Along the bottom, **MUSIC**, **ITEM >**, **< ITEM**, **PAUSE**, **< WEAPON**, **CRT** and **SAVE** do the same as F1, F3, F5, F7, the previous-weapon trigger, F9 and Ctrl+S; **KEYS** hides or shows that row while the joystick and buttons stay. **ESC** (top-left, or the Android Back button) closes an open panel, and otherwise asks whether to quit. **TOUCH** opens settings: controls on/off, size, opacity and the key row, saved in the `[Touch]` section of `LNPreserve.ini`. Menus, save slots and the toolbar respond to taps directly. With the UI hidden, double-tap the area above the game picture to bring it back. For testing on Windows or macOS with the mouse, set `desktop=1` in `[Touch]`.
+On a phone or tablet an on-screen overlay appears: a black C64-style joystick on the left (eight directions), and two red buttons on the right, **FIRE** (the # fire key) and **SPACE** (next weapon), so moving and attacking work with two thumbs. Along the bottom, **MUSIC**, **ITEM >**, **< ITEM**, **PAUSE**, **< WEAPON**, **CRT** and **SAVE** do the same as F1, F3, F5, F7, the previous-weapon trigger, F9 and Ctrl+S; **KEYS** hides or shows that row while the joystick and buttons stay. **ESC** (top-left, or the Android Back button) closes an open panel, and otherwise asks whether to quit. Menus, save slots and the toolbar respond to taps directly. With the UI hidden, double-tap the top of the screen to bring it back.
+
+**TOUCH** (top-right) opens settings: controls on/off, button size, opacity, the key row and **Game size**. **ARRANGE** lets you drag the joystick, FIRE and SPACE anywhere; RESET puts them back. Game size enlarges the picture when the UI is hidden: 100% (3x C64 pixels), 133% (4x) or 167% (5x, the largest that fits). Whole C64 pixels keep every CRT scanline the same height. Settings are saved in the `[Touch]` section of `LNPreserve.ini`. For testing on Windows or macOS with the mouse, set `desktop=1` in `[Touch]`.
 
